// The steady-state face of 00: a STANDING cross-module callsite whose
// body reads module state is NOT reactive to an outside write of that
// state — in EITHER engine. Both trace [0:false]; the epoch-1 write of
// k0 (delivered, and visible to any main-side read) produces NO
// emission from f1.
//
//   interp: Trace([0:false])
//   jit:    Trace([0:false])
//
// Mechanism (root-caused with 00): main's write targets the SIG id;
// the Module node's post-pass strips the IMPL id from the event at the
// module boundary, so f1's body ref — instantiated at main's callsite,
// holding the impl id — never sees a delivery. Only a FRESH dispatch
// (becoming-selected, first instantiation) reads the new value,
// through ctx.cached, which the Module pre-pass mutates without a
// delivery.
//
// This program AGREES today, so it is not a divergence — it is the
// semantic frame for 00's ruling: if cross-module callee reads are
// ruled fully reactive (option (b) in 00), THIS trace changes to
// [0:false, 1:true] in both engines and the file must be re-recorded.
// Until the ruling, do not promote either file to findings/.
{let v3 = &m0::k0; *v3 <- true; m0::f1(u8:2)}
// file-v1: m0.gxi
val k0: bool;
val f1: fn(a0: u8) -> bool;
// file-v1: m0.gx
let k0: bool = false;
let f1 = |v3: u8| -> bool k0
